  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para>A recreation center is offering special prices on its pool passes and gym
        memberships for the summer. On the first day of the offering, a family paid $96 for 4
        pool passes and 2 gym memberships. Later that day, an individual bought a pool pass for
        herself, a pool pass for a friend, and 1 gym membership. She paid $72.</para>
      <!--Question 1 -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Write a system of equations that represents the relationships between pool passes,
            gym memberships, and the costs. Be sure to state what each variable represents.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}4p+2g&amp;=&amp;96 \\
            2p+1g&amp;=&amp;72\end{array}\right.\),</para>
          <para>where \( p \) is the price of each pool pass and \( g \) is the price of a gym
            membership for 1 person.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Question
      2 -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Find the price of a pool pass and the price of a gym membership by solving the
            system algebraically. Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: The system has no solutions. For example: Solving by
            elimination or substitution leads to a false equation (such as \(0=24\)).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Q#3-->
    
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <!--QUESTION
          IS OUTSIDE OF INTERACTION DUE TO DESMOS-->
